 "post": {
  "title": "What if every jump went 2x higher? #shorts",
  "desc": "Jump 1 is 50 cm (1.6 ft). Every jump goes twice as high. Which jump clears a house, Tokyo Tower, and reaches space?\n*A thought experiment. Earth gravity only, no air resistance. Takeoff G assumes a 50 cm (20 in) push-off. The figure is enlarged for visibility.\n\nSources\n- Basketball hoop 3.05 m (10 ft): FIBA Official Rules 2026 Equipment https://assets.fiba.basketball/image/upload/documents-corporate-fiba-official-rules-2026-equipment-v1-0.pdf\n- Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building No.1, about 243 m: https://www.yokoso.metro.tokyo.lg.jp/kengaku/pdf/220224_totyoukengakuannai_japanes.pdf\n- Tokyo Tower 333 m: GO TOKYO https://www.gotokyo.org/jp/destinations/southern-tokyo/tokyo-tower-and-around/index.html\n- Shinkansen E5 top speed 320 km/h: JR East https://www.jreast.co.jp/train/shinkan/e5.html\n- 46.2 G human record (John Stapp, 1954): Smithsonian https://airandspace.si.edu/stories/editorial/man-behind-high-speed-safety-standards\n\nMusic: original\n#whatif #physics #science",
